WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.080
Tom Welling has been kinda quiet in Hollywood
since his gig as Clark Kent on the CW's Smallville

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.700
ended in 2011.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.480
Although he was the original superhero on
a network that's since become known for its

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.090
comic book shows, Welling has yet to capitalize
on the show's success to push into the next

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.630
stage of his acting career.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.930
Here's why Hollywood won't cast Tom Welling
anymore.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.180
Super picky

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.510
Welling spent a decade on television, which
can be very tiring for an actor, and it makes

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:29.070
sense that he'd want to take a break from
acting after having to head to the same set

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.070
for years.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:34.730
As a result, Welling's been very selective
in the roles he's taken since Smallville ended.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.370
He's only appeared in three films since the
show's 2011 finale: the Zac Efron and Billy

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.350
Bob Thornton-starring mystery drama Parkland,
the sports drama Draft Day with Kevin Costner,

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.989
and the Nicholas Sparks romance The Choice.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:48.559
Not so super reviews

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:52.829
It's not always the actor's fault when a film
doesn't do well, but it can definitely affect

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:54.739
their potential for future success.

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:59.879
Unfortunately, none of his post-Smallville
films have resonated with critics or audiences.

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:04.790
Parkland earned a 50 percent on Rotten Tomatoes
in 2013, but even worse was the fact that

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.909
it only made $1.4 million at the box office
against a $10 million budget.

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:13.630
A year later, Draft Day did slightly better,
earning a 60 percent on Rotten Tomatoes and

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:18.140
bringing in a box office haul of $29.5 million
against a budget of $25 million.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:23.880
The Choice from 2016 performed the worst of
all three with critics, earning only a 12

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.520
percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.990
It wasn't a total box office failure, though,
grossing just over $23 million worldwide against

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.829
an approximately $10 million budget.

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:37.740
Of course, none of the three films were impressive
enough to prove Welling's star power outside

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.250
of Smallville, which could make studios nervous
to cast him in big-budget films.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.270
Inexperienced

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.799
Welling was new to Hollywood when he booked
a six-episode arc on Judging Amy, which led

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:50.909
to his starring role in Smallville.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:54.640
His lack of experience was pretty obvious
in some of the earlier episodes.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:58.960
"Clark man what's wrong?"

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.720
"Clark man what's wrong?!"

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:04.120
"Ah!"

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:04.640
"Clark!"

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.530
"Woah!"

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.580
And his subsequent 10-year stint on the show
also meant that Clark Kent became Welling's

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.260
most immediately identifiable role, making
it even harder for him to break out into other

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.610
parts later.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.590
Locked in

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:22.420
The involved visual effects that Smallville
demanded meant that Welling was on set more

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.129
than most other actors would have to be, giving
him less time to pursue other projects.

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:31.730
The roles he did appear in include the ill-received
horror film The Fog with Maggie Grace and

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.099
Selma Blair, and, most notably, the role of
Charlie Baker in the Cheaper by the Dozen

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:37.099
series.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:41.370
In the end, Welling wasn't called upon to
carry a lot of dramatic weight in any of those

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.090
roles, making Smallville the most impressive
line on his resume.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.410
Behind the scenes

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.160
The former Clark Kent launched Tom Welling
Productions towards the end of Smallville's

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.840
run with the goal of spending more time behind
the camera.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.489
Welling, who began executive producing during
the later episodes of Smallville, served as

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:02.519
an executive producer on the CW's cheerleader
dramedy Hellcats in 2011.

00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:06.830
Welling also directed a few episodes of Smallville
over the years, and told the LA Times after

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.100
the show ended that directing was a new ambition.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.110
It's possible that his acting career lost
some momentum because he's focused on pursuing

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.300
other opportunities behind the camera.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.840
Failure to launch

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.470
When Welling decided that he was finally ready
to return to acting in television in 2015,

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.830
his pilot project, from Tom Welling Productions
and executive produced by the actor, ended

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.940
up not working out.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.470
Section 13 was set to follow Welling as a
CIA black ops officer who becomes a private

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:36.190
contractor in a covert organization "devoted
to carrying out the most difficult and dangerous

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.560
high-stakes assignments."

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:43.440
However, the season was crowded for CBS that
year, and the pilot was not ordered to series.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.379
How he can turn his career around

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:49.220
Welling is clearly a talented actor, as he
demonstrated during his ten years as the lead

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.320
on Smallville.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.739
But maybe instead of trying to shed his superheroic
past, he should lean in.

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:58.150
After all, it worked for one former Kryptonian,
Brandon Routh.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:02.689
After his one-and-done lead role in Superman
Returns in 2006, Routh had trouble finding

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:03.689
his footing.

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:08.750
Then, he was cast as super-scientist Ray Palmer,
better known as the Atom, in the CW's slate

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.650
of comic book shows.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.650
Now?

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.129
He's got a recurring role on Legends of Tomorrow.

00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:18.609
With more super-themed shows and movies being
announced all the time, there's no reason

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:22.380
why Welling couldn't follow suit and show
off his action and comedy chops.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:26.120
That kind of role could help him lose his
Clark Kent image while still keeping the heart

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.910
and charm that attracted audiences in the
first place.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.810
It probably won't happen faster than a speeding
bullet, but we hope to see Welling regularly

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.190
on-screen again soon.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.020
Thanks for watching!

